part 3: the extension as a peer that is not a node (bees_tempus_peer.dial and Listener)
a sample of Q's edge store: reply sample_reply entries=[] store=tempus_edge typ=tempus_sentinel
a sample of Q's sentinel store, whose one entry (the Python sentinel S) verified: reply sample_reply entries=[1:e4188f0a2cee5a46] store=tempus_sentinel typ=tempus_sentinel
a shuffle of the edge store with Q: reply shuffle_reply entries=[] store=tempus_edge typ=tempus_sentinel
a call to Q, which is no bridge: closed at=reply
the extension's listener, dialed by Q at Q's tick: served shuffle entries=[] store=tempus_edge sent=reply typ=tempus_sentinel; it was asked: shuffle of tempus_edge, 0 entries
against a peer that sends a good sample reply: reply sample_reply entries=[1:12eb7f449478f2aa] store=tempus_edge typ=tempus_edge
against a peer that sends a shuffle reply to a sample: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="the reply is not the reply of the request"
against a peer that sends a sample reply to a shuffle: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="the reply is not the reply of the request"
against a peer that sends a sample reply for another store: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="the reply is for another store"
against a peer that sends three entries to a sample of two: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="more entries than were asked for"
against a peer that sends a reply with an entry whose token another key signed: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="entry 1: the signature does not verify"
against a peer that sends the test unit's done frame: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="the reply is not the reply of the request"
against a peer that sends a reply whose atom is not UTF-8: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="bad_atom"
against a peer that sends a frame above the ceiling: refused at=reply reason="frame refused before decoding: too_large"
against a peer that sends a result with the call's req_id: reply result req_id=7231 value=5 ver=1 typ=tempus_edge
against a peer that sends a result with another req_id: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="the result is for another req_id"
against a peer that sends a result to a cast: refused at=reply typ=tempus_edge reason="the request has no reply"
against a peer that sends no reply: closed at=reply
against a peer that sends an advert under another certificate (the binding), with an expired token: refused at=advert reason="the advert's pub is not the key of the peer's TLS certificate"
against a peer that sends an advert with a tempus_sentinel token under a certificate that is not in the whitelist: refused at=advert reason="a tempus_bridge or tempus_sentinel token under a certificate that is not in the tempus whitelist"
against a peer that sends an advert with a token under another kid: refused at=advert reason="key_rotated"
against a peer that sends a wrong proof: refused at=response reason="the proof of possession does not verify"
