R ticked its edge store on its own timer and shuffled with W
the program of node R loaded no test support
part 5: the clock's choices on Python nodes; the readings are the test clock's
H (hold, continue) at 1500: a peer whose token ended at 1480, expired by 1500: closed
H read 1450, 50 s back: it holds 1500; a token that ended at 1480 (good by 1450, expired by 1500): closed; a good one: reply sample_reply entries=[] store=tempus_edge typ=tempus_sentinel
H read 1460, still behind: no line; the token that ended at 1480: closed
H could not read its clock: it goes on with its last reading, ticks, and answers: reply sample_reply entries=[0:224c0c0c5b08df0f] store=tempus_edge typ=tempus_sentinel
H read 1510 without a line, and a second failure was told again
H at 2100, its own token expired: it has stopped ticking; it still listens, and a peer that checks its advert: refused at=advert reason="the token has expired"
H was given a new token: it ticks again, and the same peer: reply sample_reply entries=[0:224c0c0c5b08df0f] store=tempus_edge typ=tempus_sentinel
H was given the producer's new key, kid k9; a peer with a token under k1: key_rotated at=challenge kid=6b39 typ=tempus_sentinel
T (stop above 60 s, pause): no sentinel answered; the join's retry timer is armed with 200 ms
T could not read its clock: it waits; a connection: closed
the join's retry fell due while T waited: it dialed nobody
T read its clock again and dialed the waiting join request at once; T holds: edge: (empty); bridge: (empty); sentinel: e4188f0a@0
T read 1470, 30 s back, inside the limit: it follows; a connection: reply sample_reply entries=[] store=tempus_edge typ=tempus_edge
T read 1370, 100 s back, above the limit: it has stopped; a connection: closed
T read 2000: it stays stopped and does not tick; a connection: closed
done
exit=0
